⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Tenskwa-Tawa
node C1 · C1 · ⟦Tenskwa-Tawa:C1:3f1493⟧

WHO   — Tenskwa-Tawa — the Red Prophet of the green silence
WHAT  — The Prophet — a visionary who builds Prophetstown and teaches the green silence, who raises a wall of fog to shield his people and leads them west across the Mizzipy after the slaughter at Tippy-Canoe.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: The Tales of Alvin Maker  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the land is alive and the white man's noise unmakes it; because a people drowned in liquor and grief can yet be called back to the green music; because some wounds the world will not let heal until they have first been seen whole.
HOW   — By visions and miracles, by the deep listening that is the green silence, by walking the living land without breaking a blade of grass — and by the terrible mercy of refusing to answer blood with blood.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  The Prophet sees what the eye cannot — that the land is one living thing, and the man who listens to its green silence will never again be alone.

spoken token : grus-nin-greith   ·   hex : 3f1493
